{%- comment -%}
  PM — HP config picker (tag-gated alternative to pm-hp-wizard.liquid). v1.5.

  v1.5 (Anuj: "why do u treat the whole card as an Add to Cart button? ...
  i only want add to cart to be triggered when add to cart button is
  clicked"): the click TARGET was too broad, not the click BEHAVIOR (v1.4's
  one-click-add stays exactly as-is) — clicking a card's price/spec/badge
  area was adding to cart same as clicking the visible pill. Fixed by making
  the card itself (cardHtml) a plain non-interactive div and moving
  data-cfgpick-pick/data-sku onto the pill (pickCtaHtml), which is now a
  real nested <button> — only clicking that button fires pickAndAdd. Rows
  deliberately NOT changed: their CTA is a 26px circle, and shrinking a
  dense list's click target down to that would be a real usability
  regression the cards don't have (their pill already spans the full card
  width). Hover feedback on the pill (darken, arrow nudge) now triggers
  from hovering the pill itself, not the whole card, to match.

  v1.4 (Anuj, immediately after v1.3 shipped: "NAH I WANT THEM TO BE ADD TO
  CART AND INITIATE ADD TO CART PROCESS! RN THEY DO NOT!"): reverted v1.3's
  select-only click back to one-click add — same as v1.2. Card/row click
  stages the build (hidden select + data-pm-add-properties) then clicks the
  real [data-pm-pdp-add] button itself, same as v1.2. CTA copy and hint text
  reverted to "Add to Cart" framing accordingly. One thing kept from v1.3
  because it's a strict improvement regardless of click-vs-select: v1.2 used
  to mark lastAddedSku ("In your cart" checkmark) synchronously the instant
  the button was clicked, which would lie if the real /cart/add.js call then
  failed (stock cap etc). v1.4 still only flips it on a CONFIRMED
  pm:cart-changed success (source 'pcard' or 'pdp').

  v1.3 (Anuj, after using v1.2 live: "when i click on any of these cards
  please do not add to cart them... only add to cart them when user clicks
  on add to cart button"): browsing/comparing a few rows was silently
  adding one cart line per click — the "less clicks" win from v1.2 turned
  into an accidental multi-add footgun in practice. Cards/rows only SELECTed
  (sync the hidden variant select + stamp data-pm-add-properties on the real
  [data-pm-pdp-add] button) — no auto-click. Reverted in v1.4 above, one
  message later — Anuj wanted the click to actually fire the add after all.

  v1.2 (Anuj: "why cant u just add them to the cart? instead of
  autoscrolling up and then asking user to click add to cart... less
  clicks and less time wasted. also like the customize button
  implementation, show the details of the build as a dropdown too"):
  v1.1's scroll-to-and-pulse-the-real-button was a half-measure — replaced
  with a genuine one-click add. Picking a card/row now: syncs the hidden
  select (unchanged), stamps `data-pm-add-properties` with the SAME shape
  the wizard already uses (every axis + "Configured total"), then clicks
  the real [data-pm-pdp-add] button itself — same proven /cart/add.js path
  the wizard's own Review-step Add to Cart already runs on, so the cart
  drawer's existing "Configured build" accordion (pm-cart-drawer.js) shows
  the same per-axis breakdown for picker-added lines as it already does
  for wizard-added ones — no cart-side changes needed, just feeding it the
  same properties shape. Card/row CTA now reads "Add to Cart →", flips to
  "In your cart ✓" for whichever config was actually just added (tracked
  separately from "is this the current page variant" — those can diverge
  right after page load, before anything's been added yet). Repeat-clicking
  the same card adds another unit on purpose — Add to Cart is additive, the
  cart drawer opening on every add is the confirmation/undo surface.
  Dropped the scroll+pulse entirely — there's no second button to point at
  anymore. (Anuj follow-up: "dont use green, make the add to cart buttons
  platinum micro orange" — CTA is rust by default now (matches the real
  Add to Cart button), navy once added, same done/current colors the
  wizard's step pips already use. No green left on the CTA.)

  Anuj: "make sure in the Product we can create a tag which basically can
  switch the ui/ux from having a customize button to this config picker
  cards / tabs". Caller (pm-product-detail.liquid) sets _hp_config_picker
  true only when a product already qualifies for the wizard (real options +
  tag "B2G" or "Customize" — vendor-agnostic) AND is additionally tagged
  "Config Picker" — remove that tag to fall straight back to the
  Customize-button wizard, no code change either way. Renders full-width
  below the whole buy area (not squeezed into the buy-box column) per
  HANDOFF-CONFIG-PICKER-UI.md.

  Why this exists instead of extending the wizard: every axis-configurator
  product resolves to real, individually-priced HP SKUs with no per-
  component price-delta data (no "+$50 for more RAM" — see
  feedback_no_price_estimation, Anuj: "leave gaps unpriced"), so a running
  total per component pick isn't possible. Instead this lets the shopper
  pick a whole real, already-priced machine directly: 3 featured cards
  (Value = cheapest, Most popular = best-stocked, Pro = priciest) plus a
  "Show N more" list of the rest — never a config without a confirmed real
  Shopify variant price (same realPrice() > 0 gate as the wizard).

  Data: reads the SAME product.metafields.hp_hermes.configurator JSON the
  wizard reads (own copy of the script-tag payload here, since the wizard
  snippet isn't rendered on this code path) plus the shared #pm-pdp-variants
  island for real price/id. Stock badge (In stock / Made to order) needs a
  real distributor qty, which variant.inventory_quantity does NOT carry —
  it's a flat placeholder (100) on every dropship SKU — so `configs[].qty`
  was baked into the metafield once via scratchpad/bake-qty-into-
  configurator.cjs, sourced from the same TD SYNNEX pull already used to
  price these variants. Purely additive key; the wizard ignores it.

  Picking a card/row does NOT reimplement price/cart math — it pushes the
  resolved SKU into the same hidden native <select data-pm-pdp-option="0">
  the wizard drives and dispatches `change` (so the PDP's existing variant-
  switch JS does all price/image/availability/cart-button sync, untouched),
  then clicks the real [data-pm-pdp-add] button itself — same /cart/add.js
  path, same qty stepper, same everything. ES5 only, matching the wizard.

  Caller gates rendering. Scoped pm-cfgpick- styles + [data-pm-cfgpicker]
  custom properties (own aliases, since the wizard's --hpw-* vars are
  scoped to its own root div, which doesn't render on this path).
  Param: product (required)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign _cfgp_wv = product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: product.variants.first -%}

<section class="pm-pdp__longblock" data-pm-cfgpicker hidden data-current-sku="{{ _cfgp_wv.sku | escape }}">
  <div class="pm-container pm-pdp__longblock-inner">
    <h2 class="pm-pdp__h2">Choose a configuration</h2>
    <p class="pm-cfgpick-hint" data-cfgpick-hint>Click a build below to add it straight to your cart.</p>
    <div class="pm-cfgpick-cards" data-cfgpick-cards></div>
    <details class="pm-cfgpick-more" data-cfgpick-more hidden>
      <summary class="pm-cfgpick-more-summary">
        <span data-cfgpick-more-label>Show more configurations</span>
        <svg class="pm-cfgpick-chev" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pm-cfgpick-rows" data-cfgpick-rows></div>
    </details>
  </div>
  {%- if product.metafields.hp_hermes.configurator -%}
    <script type="application/json" data-pm-cfgpicker-config>{{ product.metafields.hp_hermes.configurator.value | json }}</script>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>

<style>
[data-pm-cfgpicker]{
  --cfgp-navy:var(--pm-navy-deep,#0D2340);
  --cfgp-rust:var(--pm-terracotta,#A63D2F);
  --cfgp-pale:var(--pm-terracotta-pale,#F7EBE9);
  --cfgp-line:var(--pm-ink-200,#E4E7EC);
  --cfgp-ink:var(--pm-ink-800,#1D2939);
  --cfgp-mut:var(--pm-ink-500,#667085);
  --cfgp-paper:var(--pm-paper,#FBFAF7);
  --cfgp-ok:var(--pm-success,#2F7D5B);
  --cfgp-ok-bg:var(--pm-success-bg,#E8F3EC);
  --cfgp-warn:var(--pm-warning,#B5781F);
  --cfgp-warn-bg:var(--pm-warning-bg,#FAF1DF);
}
[data-pm-cfgpicker][hidden]{display:none}
[data-pm-cfgpicker] *{box-sizing:border-box}
[data-pm-cfgpicker] button{font-family:inherit}

.pm-cfgpick-hint{margin:6px 0 0;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--cfgp-mut)}
.pm-cfgpick-hint strong{color:var(--cfgp-navy);font-weight:800}

.pm-cfgpick-cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:14px;margin-top:16px}
.pm-cfgpick-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:6px;text-align:left;padding:20px;background:#fff;border:1.5px solid var(--cfgp-line);border-radius:14px;transition:border-color .12s,background .12s,box-shadow .12s}
.pm-cfgpick-card:hover{border-color:var(--cfgp-rust)}
.pm-cfgpick-card.is-active{border-color:var(--cfgp-rust);background:var(--cfgp-pale);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--cfgp-rust)}
.pm-cfgpick-tier{font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--cfgp-rust)}
.pm-cfgpick-price{font-size:22px;font-weight:800;color:var(--cfgp-navy);letter-spacing:-.01em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.pm-cfgpick-spec{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--cfgp-mut);line-height:1.4}
.pm-cfgpick-badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;margin-top:2px;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:99px;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700}
.pm-cfgpick-badge--in{color:var(--cfgp-ok);background:var(--cfgp-ok-bg)}
.pm-cfgpick-badge--made{color:var(--cfgp-warn);background:var(--cfgp-warn-bg)}
/* explicit "this is the action" affordance — cards used to read as passive
   info tiles with no visible next-step; this makes picking feel like
   pressing a real Add to Cart button. Anuj: "dont use green, make the add
   to cart buttons platinum micro orange" — rust (the same token the real
   Add to Cart button up top uses) for the actionable state, navy for
   "done" once added, same done/current pairing the wizard's own step pips
   already use — no green anywhere. is-added is its OWN state (not tied to
   is-active) — right after page load the default card IS is-active but
   nothing's been added yet, so the two must be able to disagree. */
.pm-cfgpick-pick-cta{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:7px;width:100%;margin-top:8px;padding:10px 14px;border:0;border-radius:9px;background:var(--cfgp-rust);color:#fff;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;transition:background .12s,filter .12s}
.pm-cfgpick-pick-cta:hover{filter:brightness(.93)}
.pm-cfgpick-pick-cta.is-added{background:var(--cfgp-navy)}
.pm-cfgpick-pick-cta svg{transition:transform .15s ease;flex:none}
.pm-cfgpick-pick-cta:hover svg{transform:translateX(3px)}
.pm-cfgpick-row-cta{flex:none;display:grid;place-items:center;width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--cfgp-rust);color:#fff;transition:background .12s,filter .12s}
.pm-cfgpick-row:hover .pm-cfgpick-row-cta{filter:brightness(.93)}
.pm-cfgpick-row-cta.is-added{background:var(--cfgp-navy)}

.pm-cfgpick-more{margin-top:14px;border:1.5px solid var(--cfgp-line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden}
.pm-cfgpick-more[hidden]{display:none}
.pm-cfgpick-more-summary{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;padding:14px;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--cfgp-navy);user-select:none}
.pm-cfgpick-more-summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.pm-cfgpick-chev{transition:transform .15s ease;flex:none}
.pm-cfgpick-more[open] .pm-cfgpick-chev{transform:rotate(180deg)}
.pm-cfgpick-rows{border-top:1px solid var(--cfgp-line)}
.pm-cfgpick-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;width:100%;padding:12px 16px;background:#fff;border:0;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--cfgp-line);cursor:pointer;text-align:left;transition:background .12s}
.pm-cfgpick-row:last-child{border-bottom:0}
.pm-cfgpick-row:hover{background:var(--cfgp-paper)}
.pm-cfgpick-row.is-active{background:var(--cfgp-pale)}
.pm-cfgpick-row-spec{flex:1;min-width:0;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--cfgp-ink)}
.pm-cfgpick-row-price{flex:none;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:var(--cfgp-navy);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
</style>

<script>
(function () {
  'use strict';
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') { document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init); } else { init(); }

  function init() {
    var root = document.querySelector('[data-pm-cfgpicker]');
    if (!root) return;
    var cfgEl = root.querySelector('[data-pm-cfgpicker-config]');
    var varsEl = document.getElementById('pm-pdp-variants');
    if (!cfgEl || !varsEl) return;

    var CONFIG = null, VARS = [];
    try { CONFIG = JSON.parse(cfgEl.textContent); VARS = JSON.parse(varsEl.textContent); } catch (e) { return; }
    if (!CONFIG || !CONFIG.axes || !CONFIG.configs || !CONFIG.configs.length || !VARS.length) return;

    var AXES = [];
    for (var _k in CONFIG.axes) { if (CONFIG.axes.hasOwnProperty(_k)) AXES.push(_k); }
    var SPEC_AXES = [];
    for (var _a = 0; _a < AXES.length; _a++) { if (!/^os$/i.test(AXES[_a])) SPEC_AXES.push(AXES[_a]); }
    if (!AXES.length) return;

    function esc(s) { return String(s == null ? '' : s).replace(/[&<>"]/g, function (c) { return { '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' }[c]; }); }
    function money(cents) {
      try { return new Intl.NumberFormat(undefined, { style: 'currency', currency: (window.Shopify && Shopify.currency && Shopify.currency.active) || 'USD' }).format(cents / 100); }
      catch (e) { return '$' + (cents / 100).toFixed(2); }
    }
    /* same gate as pm-hp-wizard.liquid: an unpriced variant's real Shopify
       price is `0`, not absent — never treat that as a usable price */
    function realPrice(v) { return (v && typeof v.price === 'number' && v.price > 0) ? v.price : null; }
    function variantForSku(sku) {
      for (var i = 0; i < VARS.length; i++) { if (VARS[i].sku === sku) return VARS[i]; }
      return null;
    }
    /* reverse of the above — needed because the hidden select's real value
       is option1 (see pickAndAdd()), not necessarily the bare sku, so any
       code reacting to the select's OWN change events (below) must translate
       back to a sku before touching currentSku, or card/row active-state
       matching (keyed on sku) silently stops working after the first pick */
    function skuForOption1(val) {
      for (var i = 0; i < VARS.length; i++) { if (VARS[i].option1 === val) return VARS[i].sku; }
      return val;
    }

    /* "AMD Ryzen™ 5 8600G (up to 5.0 GHz ...)" -> "Ryzen 5 8600G"
       "2 x 16 GB" -> "32GB" (total capacity, not module count)
       "512 GB PCIe® Gen4 NVMe™ TLC M.2 SSD" -> "512GB"
       "AMD Radeon™ RX 6300 Graphics (2 GB GDDR6 dedicated)" -> "Radeon RX 6300" */
    function shortSpec(raw) {
      var s = String(raw == null ? '' : raw).trim();
      var ram = /^(\d+)\s*x\s*(\d+)\s*GB$/i.exec(s);
      if (ram) return (Number(ram[1]) * Number(ram[2])) + 'GB';
      var sto = /^(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)\s*(GB|TB)\b/i.exec(s);
      if (sto && /SSD|HDD|NVMe|eMMC/i.test(s)) return sto[1] + sto[2].toUpperCase();
      s = s.replace(/\b(AMD|Intel|NVIDIA)\b\s*/gi, '').replace(/[™®]/g, '');
      s = s.replace(/\s*\([^)]*\)\s*$/, '');
      s = s.replace(/\s+Graphics$/i, '');
      return s.trim();
    }
    function specLine(attrs) {
      var parts = [];
      for (var i = 0; i < SPEC_AXES.length; i++) {
        var v = attrs[SPEC_AXES[i]];
        if (v) parts.push(shortSpec(v));
      }
      return parts.join(' · ');
    }

    /* real, confirmed-price configs only — never list an estimate */
    var priced = [];
    for (var i = 0; i < CONFIG.configs.length; i++) {
      var c = CONFIG.configs[i];
      var v = variantForSku(c.sku);
      var price = realPrice(v);
      if (price == null) continue;
      priced.push({ sku: c.sku, price: price, qty: (typeof c.qty === 'number' ? c.qty : 0), attributes: c.attributes, variantId: v.id });
    }
    if (!priced.length) return; /* nothing confirmed — leave the section hidden, same fail-closed posture as the wizard */

    var byPrice = priced.slice().sort(function (a, b) { return a.price - b.price; });
    var valueCfg = byPrice[0];
    var proCfg = byPrice[byPrice.length - 1];
    var seen = {}; seen[valueCfg.sku] = true; seen[proCfg.sku] = true;
    var remaining = priced.filter(function (c) { return !seen[c.sku]; });
    var popularCfg = null;
    if (remaining.length) {
      popularCfg = remaining.slice().sort(function (a, b) { return b.qty - a.qty; })[0];
      seen[popularCfg.sku] = true;
    }
    if (proCfg.sku === valueCfg.sku) proCfg = null; /* only one distinct confirmed config total */

    var featured = [];
    if (valueCfg) featured.push({ tier: 'Value', cfg: valueCfg });
    if (popularCfg) featured.push({ tier: 'Most popular', cfg: popularCfg });
    if (proCfg) featured.push({ tier: 'Pro', cfg: proCfg });
    var rest = priced.filter(function (c) { return !seen[c.sku]; });

    var cardsEl = root.querySelector('[data-cfgpick-cards]');
    var moreEl = root.querySelector('[data-cfgpick-more]');
    var rowsEl = root.querySelector('[data-cfgpick-rows]');
    var moreLabelEl = root.querySelector('[data-cfgpick-more-label]');
    var selectEl = document.querySelector('[data-pm-pdp-option="0"]');
    var currentSku = root.getAttribute('data-current-sku');
    var lastAddedSku = null; /* distinct from currentSku — set only once the real Add to Cart button confirms a successful add */

    function badgeHtml(qty) {
      return qty > 0
        ? '<span class="pm-cfgpick-badge pm-cfgpick-badge--in">In stock</span>'
        : '<span class="pm-cfgpick-badge pm-cfgpick-badge--made">Made to order</span>';
    }
    var ARROW_SVG = '<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>';
    var CHECK_SVG = '<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>';
    /* Anuj: "why do u treat the whole card as an Add to Cart button? ...
       i only want add to cart to be triggered when add to cart button is
       clicked". The card itself (title/price/spec/badge) is now a plain
       non-interactive div — ONLY the pill below is a real <button>
       carrying data-cfgpick-pick/data-sku, so clicking the price or spec
       text no longer adds anything. Rows are intentionally left as
       whole-row buttons: their CTA is a small 26px circle, and shrinking
       the click target down to just that on a dense list would be a real
       usability regression the cards don't have (their pill already spans
       the full card width). Flips to a checkmark once THAT config was
       actually added via this same button (added !== is-active: right
       after page load the default card is active but nothing's been added
       yet). */
    function pickCtaHtml(sku, added) {
      return '<button type="button" class="pm-cfgpick-pick-cta' + (added ? ' is-added' : '') + '" data-cfgpick-pick data-sku="' + esc(sku) + '"><span>' + (added ? 'In your cart' : 'Add to Cart') + '</span>' + (added ? CHECK_SVG : ARROW_SVG) + '</button>';
    }
    function rowCtaHtml(added) {
      return '<span class="pm-cfgpick-row-cta' + (added ? ' is-added' : '') + '">' + (added ? CHECK_SVG : ARROW_SVG) + '</span>';
    }
    function cardHtml(item) {
      var isCurrent = item.cfg.sku === currentSku;
      var wasAdded = item.cfg.sku === lastAddedSku;
      return '<div class="pm-cfgpick-card' + (isCurrent ? ' is-active' : '') + '">'
        + '<span class="pm-cfgpick-tier">' + esc(item.tier) + '</span>'
        + '<span class="pm-cfgpick-price">' + money(item.cfg.price) + '</span>'
        + '<span class="pm-cfgpick-spec">' + esc(specLine(item.cfg.attributes)) + '</span>'
        + badgeHtml(item.cfg.qty)
        + pickCtaHtml(item.cfg.sku, wasAdded)
        + '</div>';
    }
    function rowHtml(cfg) {
      var isCurrent = cfg.sku === currentSku;
      var wasAdded = cfg.sku === lastAddedSku;
      return '<button type="button" class="pm-cfgpick-row' + (isCurrent ? ' is-active' : '') + '" data-cfgpick-pick data-sku="' + esc(cfg.sku) + '">'
        + '<span class="pm-cfgpick-row-spec">' + esc(specLine(cfg.attributes)) + '</span>'
        + '<span class="pm-cfgpick-row-price">' + money(cfg.price) + '</span>'
        + badgeHtml(cfg.qty)
        + rowCtaHtml(wasAdded)
        + '</button>';
    }
    var DEFAULT_HINT = 'Click a build below to add it straight to your cart.';
    function updateHint() {
      var hintEl = root.querySelector('[data-cfgpick-hint]');
      if (!hintEl) return;
      if (!lastAddedSku) { hintEl.innerHTML = DEFAULT_HINT; return; }
      var added = null;
      for (var i = 0; i < priced.length; i++) { if (priced[i].sku === lastAddedSku) { added = priced[i]; break; } }
      hintEl.innerHTML = added
        ? '<strong>' + money(added.price) + '</strong> added to your cart — pick another build to add more.'
        : DEFAULT_HINT;
    }
    function render() {
      cardsEl.innerHTML = featured.map(cardHtml).join('');
      if (rest.length) {
        moreEl.hidden = false;
        rowsEl.innerHTML = rest.map(rowHtml).join('');
        if (moreLabelEl) moreLabelEl.textContent = 'Show ' + rest.length + ' more configuration' + (rest.length === 1 ? '' : 's');
      } else {
        moreEl.hidden = true;
      }
      updateHint();
    }

    /* Same shape pm-hp-wizard.liquid's syncSelects() stamps onto
       data-pm-add-properties: every axis value + "Configured total". The
       cart drawer (pm-cart-drawer.js) already renders any line's real
       Shopify `properties` as a "Configured build" accordion — built for
       the wizard, reused as-is here, no cart-side change needed. */
    function buildPropsFor(cfgEntry) {
      var props = {};
      for (var i = 0; i < AXES.length; i++) {
        var v = cfgEntry.attributes[AXES[i]];
        if (v != null) props[AXES[i]] = v;
      }
      props['Configured total'] = money(cfgEntry.price);
      return props;
    }
    /* Anuj (v1.3 → v1.4, immediate reversal): "NAH I WANT THEM TO BE ADD TO
       CART AND INITIATE ADD TO CART PROCESS! RN THEY DO NOT!" — back to one
       click doing the whole job. Stage the build (sync the hidden select —
       Option1 Value is NOT always the bare SKU on the v2 G9 import, so
       resolve the REAL option1 string from VARS rather than assuming it —
       and stamp data-pm-add-properties), then click the REAL
       [data-pm-pdp-add] button itself, same as v1.2. Kept from v1.3 though:
       lastAddedSku/"In your cart" now only flips on the pm:cart-changed
       listener below confirming a genuine success, instead of assuming the
       click always works — v1.2 marked it added optimistically, which was
       wrong if the real /cart/add.js call failed (stock cap, etc). */
    function pickAndAdd(sku) {
      var cfgEntry = null;
      for (var i = 0; i < priced.length; i++) { if (priced[i].sku === sku) { cfgEntry = priced[i]; break; } }
      if (!cfgEntry) return;
      currentSku = sku;
      if (selectEl) {
        var v = variantForSku(sku);
        var optVal = (v && typeof v.option1 === 'string') ? v.option1 : sku;
        if (selectEl.value !== optVal) {
          selectEl.value = optVal;
          var ev; try { ev = new Event('change', { bubbles: true }); } catch (e) { ev = document.createEvent('Event'); ev.initEvent('change', true, true); }
          selectEl.dispatchEvent(ev);
        }
      }
      var addBtn = document.querySelector('[data-pm-pdp-add]');
      if (addBtn) addBtn.setAttribute('data-pm-add-properties', JSON.stringify(buildPropsFor(cfgEntry)));
      render();
      if (addBtn && !addBtn.disabled) addBtn.click();
    }
    function onPick(e) {
      var btn = e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('[data-cfgpick-pick]') : null;
      if (!btn) return;
      pickAndAdd(btn.getAttribute('data-sku'));
    }
    cardsEl.addEventListener('click', onPick);
    rowsEl.addEventListener('click', onPick);
    if (selectEl) {
      selectEl.addEventListener('change', function () {
        var sku = skuForOption1(selectEl.value);
        if (sku !== currentSku) { currentSku = sku; render(); }
      });
    }
    /* lastAddedSku (drives the "In your cart" checkmark) only flips on a
       CONFIRMED /cart/add.js success for the real button — source 'pcard'
       (assets/pm-add-to-cart.js, the qty=1 path) or 'pdp' (this section's
       own inline qty>1/bundle handler). Every other pm:cart-changed source
       (drawer qty/remove, Quotify's separate quote cart, the paused HPE
       flow) is NOT this config being added, so it's ignored — otherwise
       e.g. removing an unrelated cart line would falsely check this card. */
    document.addEventListener('pm:cart-changed', function (e) {
      var src = e.detail && e.detail.source;
      if (src !== 'pcard' && src !== 'pdp') return;
      lastAddedSku = currentSku;
      render();
    });

    render();
    root.hidden = false;
  }
})();
</script>
